    "background_story": "Spencer was a talented watchmaker who lived in a small village nestled in the rolling hills of the countryside. Despite his diminutive stature, he had a giant's presence in the world of horology. His tiny hands moved with precision and delicacy, crafting intricate timepieces that were sought after by collectors from far and wide. Spencer's workshop was a marvel of miniature machinery and tools, each one carefully adapted to his unique needs. His diminutive size allowed him to focus on the smallest details, and his creations were renowned for their accuracy and beauty. As he worked, Spencer would often joke that his small size was actually a blessing in disguise, allowing him to create masterpieces that others could only dream of.",
